  * Release CaramOS 1.4.0.
  * Run all pending timestamp migrations by migration ID ledger.
  * CaramOS Xfce, a light edition for 2 GB computers and school computer labs
    (a Tin học teacher's request): its own ISO, built from Linux Mint 22.3
    Xfce. It speaks English by default, as the Tin học textbooks use Windows'
    English words; Vietnamese typing is unchanged, and choosing Vietnamese in
    the installer still gives Vietnamese. It has the three taskbar islands of
    the Cinnamon edition (xfce4-docklike-plugin), its own Control Center
    (sound, network, Bluetooth, battery, power mode, dark mode, accent colour
    and Night Light, in the taskbar through xfce4-caramos-plugin), the level
    display of the sound keys, Files (Nemo) as the file manager, the five
    CaramOS wallpapers, Driver Check and the Update Center. os-release and
    lsb-release name the edition.
  * Migrations say which desktop they are for ("desktops" in the manifest):
    the 14 that change only Cinnamon are skipped on the Xfce edition, and the
    Update Center does not list them there.
  * The Xfce edition uses over 100 MB less memory: calendar reminders and the
    Bluetooth icon start only when needed; System Reports, the Flameshot
    daemon, the print queue icon, xiccd and colord, GNOME Online Accounts,
    fwupd's twice-daily refresh and ModemManager no longer run in the
    background; xfwm4 follows the screen through XPresent instead of OpenGL. A
    2 GB computer shows about 612 MB in Task Manager after boot.
  * Xfce: the launchers on the Desktop open at the first double-click (Xfce
    4.18 asked whether to trust them, then failed with "Timeout was reached"),
    and the power button asks what to do, as on Cinnamon.
  * Files: right-click > New > Folder (Mới > Thư mục on the Cinnamon edition),
    with Word, Excel, PowerPoint and text templates, as in Windows and the
    school textbooks; new installs show the folder tree in the left pane, like
    Windows Explorer.
  * Computer Lab (Phòng máy): classroom management with Veyon or Epoptes in
    one click. The teacher's computer shows a 6-digit code; students'
    computers find it on the school network, check the code and set themselves
    up.
  * Word, Excel and PowerPoint files open in the right app: without an office
    suite, opening one offers ONLYOFFICE, WPS Office or LibreOffice from the
    App Center instead of only showing its folder, and .zip files open in the
    archive manager.
  * The daily Vietnam wallpaper works on Xfce (Desktop settings > Folder),
    next to a "CaramOS" folder with the five CaramOS wallpapers.
  * The Control Center's sliders on Cinnamon are longer, and their track shows
    in the dark theme.
  * The boot-success timer no longer fires every 30 seconds after an upgrade
    of this package until the next boot.

