caramos-ota (1.3.7-0caramos1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Release CaramOS 1.3.7.
  * Run all pending timestamp migrations by migration ID ledger.
  * Driver Check: Canon CAPT laser printers (LBP2900/LBP2900B and family).
    They need a CAPT driver. Without one the automatic printer setup gave
    them an unrelated PostScript driver (an LBP2900 got an HP Designjet
    one), and the queue reported jobs as printed while nothing came out.
    A udev rule now skips the automatic setup for these printers until a
    driver that fits is installed. Driver Check has a "Printer" area, and
    for the models captdriver drives it installs printer-driver-captdriver
    (new in the PPA) with one click. That package switches wrong queues to
    captdriver and sets up a plugged-in printer. For the models only
    Canon's driver drives, Driver Check offers to ask for help.
  * Driver Check speaks up as soon as such a printer is plugged in, through
    a systemd user unit the udev rule starts, instead of at the next login.
    A problem of a device that is unplugged is no longer told as solved at
    the next login, nor told again when the device comes back.
  * Driver Check: the page of a failed driver install has an "Ask for
    help" button, like the App Center's and the Update Center's, and the
    request carries what the helper printed (driver-install.log).
  * Help requests from Driver Check and Feedback & Help carry printer.log
    when the computer has a USB printer or a print queue: the printers,
    queues and jobs, the automatic printer setup and the end of CUPS's
    error_log, without serial numbers or document names.

